      "keyInsight": "Most people think their spine is designed to twist and bend like a fishing rod under heavy loads. That is a dangerous trap. In reality, your spine is a structural concrete pillar meant to transmit raw horsepower from your engine to your wheels. When your trunk goes soft, power bleeds out everywhere, exactly like stepping on the gas in a sports car with a cracked, rusty frame. You do not fix a bad back by doing random crunches or stretching until you snap. You fix it by learning how to lock your pelvis and ribcage together into an unshakable vault. Squeeze your glutes, pull your ribs down, and stiffen your belly like preparing for a heavy bag strike. Once your midline is locked, your hips and shoulders can generate monstrous force without crushing your delicate spinal discs.",
